        <img loading="lazy" src="https://res.cloudinary.com/dlhqdgmih/image/upload/q_auto,f_auto/v1768256600/PXL_20241206_001021963.MP_g6jdgp.jpg" alt="Sauna detail" class="full-width-image reveal" width="1446" height="1920">

        <!-- 6. Comparison LEDGER (Jen B7 mini-spec) -- archetype E, tight tier,
             on ground, --hold containment.

             It was an asymmetric Essay (archetype D) for the length of B4-B6,
             and before that three cards carrying 21 tick/cross bullets. The
             ledger is the third and last form: the argument is a COMPARISON, and
             a comparison read as prose makes the reader hold three columns of
             fact in their head while the paragraph walks them through it one
             clause at a time. A table hands them the same facts already aligned.
             The page order becomes A→E→C→E→C→E→B→C→G, nine sections; the D is
             gone and the 60-side plate with it.

             EVERY CELL IS SOURCED. Each one traces to a bullet in the three
             comparison cards as they stood at ab83ed6 (saunas.njk:110-163) --
             this batch re-tabulates copy, it does not write claims. The two
             temperatures and the two lifespans below come from those cards and
             from nowhere else; in particular they are NOT models.json material,
             which carries size, capacity and price only, so the round-trip gate
             has nothing to say about this table and needs no extension.

             Two cells are deliberately EMPTY (en dash): the cards recorded no
             heat-retention claim for infrared and no evidence claim for barrels.
             An empty cell is the honest rendering of "the source says nothing
             here". Inventing a line to square the grid is exactly the failure
             this comment exists to prevent. -->
        <section class="container section--tight">
            <div class="ledger-lede reveal">
                <h2 class="ledger-lede__heading">Why Traditional Finnish Saunas?</h2>
                <p>Ours are built the way a house is built: a framed envelope, insulated to R-13 or better, sealed behind a vapour barrier, clad in Western Red Cedar inside and metal outside. That construction is what makes proper löyly possible at 80 to 100°C, holds the heat instead of pouring it into the yard, and keeps the whole thing standing outdoors for twenty-five years and more. The usual alternatives cannot do that.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="compare-ledger reveal">
                <!-- Labels carry classes for the same instrument reason the model
                     index records at :61 -- a dom-integrity whitelist entry names
                     a node by a substring of its ATTRIBUTES, so an attribute-less
                     span cannot be declared. -->
                <div class="compare-ledger__head" aria-hidden="false">
                    <span class="compare-ledger__label compare-ledger__label--dimension"></span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__label compare-ledger__label--ours">Our Finnish</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__label compare-ledger__label--barrel">Barrel</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__label compare-ledger__label--infrared">Infrared</span>
                </div>

                <div class="compare-ledger__row">
                    <span class="compare-ledger__dimension">Construction</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value compare-ledger__value--ours"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Ours</span>Fully insulated envelope (R-13+ walls), 2x4 framing with vapour barrier, cedar cladding inside and metal outside</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Barrel</span>No insulation, single-wall stave construction with metal bands, wood exposed inside and out</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Infrared</span>Often made with cheap materials</span>
                </div>

                <div class="compare-ledger__row">
                    <span class="compare-ledger__dimension">Heat &amp; löyly</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value compare-ledger__value--ours"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Ours</span>Proper löyly (steam) at 80–100°C</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Barrel</span>Difficult to achieve proper heat</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Infrared</span>Heats your body, not the air. No steam (löyly) possible, max temp around 60°C</span>
                </div>

                <div class="compare-ledger__row">
                    <span class="compare-ledger__dimension">Heat retention</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value compare-ledger__value--ours"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Ours</span>Heats evenly, retains heat efficiently</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Barrel</span>Loses heat quickly in cold weather, higher energy costs to operate</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value compare-ledger__value--empty"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Infrared</span>–</span>
                </div>

                <div class="compare-ledger__row">
                    <span class="compare-ledger__dimension">Lifespan outdoors</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value compare-ledger__value--ours"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Ours</span>Built to last 25+ years outdoors</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Barrel</span>5–10 year lifespan typical</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Infrared</span>Indoor use only</span>
                </div>

                <div class="compare-ledger__row">
                    <span class="compare-ledger__dimension">Evidence</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value compare-ledger__value--ours"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Ours</span>Proven health benefits over millennia</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value compare-ledger__value--empty"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Barrel</span>–</span>
                    <span class="compare-ledger__value"><span class="compare-ledger__source">Infrared</span>Unproven long-term health claims</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="compare-ledger__link reveal"><a href="/faq/" class="link--accent">The full comparison →</a></p>
        </section>

